You're not hiding behind lame excuses

271
00:23:23,298 --> 00:23:26,218
like panic disorder and depression
after stealing someone's life.

272
00:23:29,888 --> 00:23:31,223
Hey, are you crazy?

273
00:23:31,806 --> 00:23:32,682
Are you insane?

274
00:23:33,517 --> 00:23:35,477
Get a grip, man.

275
00:23:35,560 --> 00:23:36,561
You…

276
00:23:37,646 --> 00:23:39,397
You're the bad guy, you bastard!

277
00:23:41,483 --> 00:23:43,443
You don't remember stealing my notebooks?

278
00:23:44,319 --> 00:23:46,655
Everything in your novels
came from my notebooks.

279
00:23:46,738 --> 00:23:49,366
You're the fake university student,
you bastard!

280
00:23:50,408 --> 00:23:51,243
Those were

281
00:23:51,910 --> 00:23:53,119
my notebooks…

282
00:23:53,620 --> 00:23:54,454
What is it?

283
00:23:55,372 --> 00:23:57,165
Why are you trailing off? Huh?

284
00:23:57,249 --> 00:23:58,375
You're not so confident?

285
00:24:00,669 --> 00:24:03,004
Min-yeong was my junior in the department.

286
00:24:05,882 --> 00:24:07,300
She went out with me.

287
00:24:07,384 --> 00:24:09,886
That's all from your novel,
you crazy bastard!

288
00:24:09,970 --> 00:24:12,681
That's not reality, you bastard!

289
00:24:16,476 --> 00:24:17,394
Why?

290
00:24:17,894 --> 00:24:19,312
Why do you want to be me?

291
00:24:20,272 --> 00:24:21,147
Huh?

292
00:24:26,903 --> 00:24:28,280
Now I remember.

293
00:24:38,999 --> 00:24:41,543
Now I understand
why I couldn't write anything

294
00:24:42,294 --> 00:24:43,670
for some time now.

295
00:24:44,963 --> 00:24:46,423
None of it

296
00:24:47,090 --> 00:24:49,426
was ever mine to begin with.

297
00:24:58,977 --> 00:25:01,104
After barely overcoming my panic disorder,

298
00:25:01,688 --> 00:25:03,940
I wanted to become
a better version of myself,

299
00:25:04,733 --> 00:25:07,652
like my mom always told me.

300
00:25:08,153 --> 00:25:10,822
INTERCOLLEGIATE LITERATURE CLUB
RECRUITING NEW MEMBERS

301
00:25:10,905 --> 00:25:12,115
Hey, guys. Listen up.

302
00:25:13,116 --> 00:25:14,743
We got a new member today.

303
00:25:14,826 --> 00:25:16,953
Hello, I'm Je Moon-jae.

304
00:25:17,037 --> 00:25:18,747
It's very nice to meet you all.

305
00:25:21,207 --> 00:25:22,250
Have a seat.

306
00:25:50,528 --> 00:25:51,529
You eat first.

307
00:25:55,033 --> 00:25:56,201
-It's good, right?
-Yeah.

308
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:58,745
I'll eat the burnt part again.

309
00:25:58,828 --> 00:26:00,789
Hey, looking good, you two.

310
00:26:01,456 --> 00:26:02,290
Huh?

311
00:26:03,458 --> 00:26:04,584
Something might happen.

312
00:26:06,961 --> 00:26:08,713
Stop drinking. You're already drunk.

313
00:26:14,427 --> 00:26:16,012
Min-yeong. Let's talk.

314
00:26:16,513 --> 00:26:18,348
-You're drunk. Talk tomorrow.
-Fuck.

315
00:26:18,431 --> 00:26:19,808
Let go, you bastard.

316
00:26:19,891 --> 00:26:20,725
What are you?

317
00:26:20,809 --> 00:26:22,394
You said you two weren't a thing.

318
00:26:23,478 --> 00:26:24,729
We're dating.

319
00:26:24,813 --> 00:26:29,567
We kept it a secret at the club
because it'd be awkward if people knew.

320
00:26:33,238 --> 00:26:34,280
Since when?

321
00:26:35,448 --> 00:26:36,866
Since before you asked me.

322
00:26:39,160 --> 00:26:43,498
Fuck. You two shouldn't toy with people.

323
00:26:43,581 --> 00:26:44,791
Huh?

324
00:27:10,150 --> 00:27:11,985
You are just jealous of me.

325
00:27:12,485 --> 00:27:15,655
You're dying of jealousy
because you want to be me.

326
00:27:17,240 --> 00:27:18,324
Aren't you?

327
00:27:20,285 --> 00:27:21,786
Shut up.

328
00:27:21,870 --> 00:27:23,580
I said shut up.

329
00:28:01,159 --> 00:28:01,993
I was

330
00:28:03,286 --> 00:28:04,913
the fake university student?

331
00:28:07,749 --> 00:28:09,125
I never dated Min-yeong…

332
00:28:11,377 --> 00:28:13,338
and all my novels were yours?

333
00:28:27,101 --> 00:28:28,812
Were you always crazy?

334
00:28:28,895 --> 00:28:30,939
Or did the meds make you crazy?

335
00:28:31,523 --> 00:28:32,899
Yu-min.

336
00:28:34,442 --> 00:28:35,610
Then was I…

337
00:28:38,696 --> 00:28:40,240
Was I the Rat?

338
00:28:48,540 --> 00:28:51,084
You weren't supposed to show up here.

339
00:28:52,252 --> 00:28:56,005
That beach.
You should've come to that vacation home.

340
00:28:56,089 --> 00:28:58,258
I should've disappeared there forever,

341
00:28:59,384 --> 00:29:02,178
and you should've been exposed
to the world as the real Rat.

342
00:29:02,262 --> 00:29:03,555
That was our ending.

343
00:29:14,274 --> 00:29:15,108
Sir!

344
00:29:16,442 --> 00:29:17,527
Sir!

345
00:29:18,820 --> 00:29:20,321
-Go get the master key.
-Sir.

346
00:29:20,405 --> 00:29:21,239
Sir!

347
00:29:21,322 --> 00:29:22,991
Do you know what's going on?

348
00:29:23,074 --> 00:29:24,534
Open up! Sir! Are you okay?

349
00:29:24,617 --> 00:29:26,411
One of us

350
00:29:28,162 --> 00:29:30,582
has to disappear forever right here.

351
00:29:31,082 --> 00:29:33,751
Before they open the door!

352
00:29:33,835 --> 00:29:34,961
Sir, are you okay?

353
00:29:36,713 --> 00:29:37,547
Sir, open up!

354
00:29:37,630 --> 00:29:39,132
Just die.

355
00:29:41,301 --> 00:29:42,927
I'll live as Je Moon-jae.

356
00:30:34,479 --> 00:30:36,773
Everyone should be out.
Why can't we see him?

357
00:30:36,856 --> 00:30:38,608
You checked the passenger list, right?

358
00:30:38,691 --> 00:30:41,819
I did. I checked
that writer Je Moon-jae was on board.

359
00:30:50,036 --> 00:30:52,580
WRITER JE MOON-JAE

360
00:31:27,907 --> 00:31:28,950
What's going on?

361
00:31:29,033 --> 00:31:31,077
He said there was an accident last night.

362
00:31:32,036 --> 00:31:33,204
What accident?

363
00:31:40,253 --> 00:31:42,422
He snuck on board that ship.

364
00:31:42,922 --> 00:31:44,173
To kill me.

365
00:31:44,257 --> 00:31:45,299
We checked the CCTV.

366
00:31:45,883 --> 00:31:47,802
There was someone who looked like him.

367
00:31:50,513 --> 00:31:51,806
What is he talking about?

368
00:31:51,889 --> 00:31:52,724
And?

369
00:31:54,517 --> 00:31:55,893
He fell into the ocean.

370
00:31:56,644 --> 00:31:59,313
He tried to throw me out the window,
but fell himself.

371
00:32:01,149 --> 00:32:03,401
I think he thought killing me
would make him me.

372
00:32:22,754 --> 00:32:26,174
I'm glad you found my uncle.
We should do the DNA test right away.

373
00:32:27,884 --> 00:32:29,010
In due time.

374
00:32:30,094 --> 00:32:31,846
Not that I think we need to.

375
00:32:32,722 --> 00:32:35,224
I told you, I'm Je Moon-jae.

376
00:32:35,308 --> 00:32:38,311
Even if he'd killed me,
he couldn't have proven he was me anyway.

377
00:32:38,394 --> 00:32:40,730
He wouldn't have known
you'd find my uncle.

378
00:32:44,692 --> 00:32:46,652
Thanks to you, I'll clear my name.

379
00:32:48,279 --> 00:32:49,113
The button.

380
00:32:51,115 --> 00:32:54,077
-What?
-Button up your shirt all the way.

381
00:32:56,496 --> 00:32:58,039
That's how he wears it.

382
00:33:14,639 --> 00:33:16,599
Why are you going this far?

383
00:33:22,563 --> 00:33:24,023
I don't follow…

384
00:33:24,816 --> 00:33:27,693
You can drop the act. I'm not recording.

385
00:33:29,779 --> 00:33:31,280
Isn't killing the fake enough?

386
00:33:31,364 --> 00:33:32,365
Why?

387
00:33:33,074 --> 00:33:35,076
Why are you pretending to be the fake one?

388
00:33:36,327 --> 00:33:39,831
Was there something else he had
that you wanted?

389
00:33:45,586 --> 00:33:48,464
You always take someone's place…

390
00:36:09,230 --> 00:36:10,314
Did you really

391
00:36:11,691 --> 00:36:13,401
want to be me that badly?

392
00:36:16,737 --> 00:36:18,739
I don't think I wanted to be you.

393
00:36:20,199 --> 00:36:21,951
I think I wanted to be myself.

394
00:36:23,369 --> 00:36:24,787
A better version of myself.

395
00:36:44,015 --> 00:36:45,266
This isn't the end.

396
00:36:46,767 --> 00:36:48,644
You won't be able to handle it.

397
00:37:51,082 --> 00:37:52,166
Long ago…

398
00:37:55,044 --> 00:37:56,754
my mom told me this all the time.

399
00:37:59,715 --> 00:38:03,177
"You have to be a better Je Moon-jae
than the old Moon-jae."

400
00:38:04,220 --> 00:38:05,471
Now…

401
00:38:07,473 --> 00:38:09,350
I understand what it meant.

402
00:38:12,436 --> 00:38:15,606
I heard you were Je Moon-jae once.

403
00:38:22,738 --> 00:38:24,907
I think there's a misunderstanding here.

404
00:38:24,990 --> 00:38:26,992
That place was always mine.

405
00:38:28,494 --> 00:38:30,538
I didn't take it from you.

406
00:38:40,798 --> 00:38:42,675
Keep that place all to yourself.

407
00:38:43,509 --> 00:38:44,468
Why would I care?

408
00:38:45,177 --> 00:38:47,179
Let's never cross paths again.

409
00:40:02,379 --> 00:40:04,298
Oh, you changed your style.

410
00:40:06,133 --> 00:40:07,218
Looks fucking awful.

411
00:40:14,600 --> 00:40:15,601
Are you hurt badly?

412
00:40:15,684 --> 00:40:17,686
It just grazed me, you punk.

413
00:40:19,813 --> 00:40:20,814
And the hospital?

414
00:40:23,025 --> 00:40:23,859
Did you eat?

415
00:40:42,169 --> 00:40:43,879
You're not popping your meds anymore?

416
00:40:45,631 --> 00:40:47,258
No, not anymore.

417
00:40:47,841 --> 00:40:48,842
I'm all better.

418
00:40:53,347 --> 00:40:54,557
What's with your arm?

419
00:40:56,141 --> 00:40:58,561
I don't fucking know.
It just doesn't move.

420
00:40:59,061 --> 00:41:01,355
Then you should go to the hospital.

421
00:41:01,981 --> 00:41:03,732
Hospital? You bastard.

422
00:41:03,816 --> 00:41:05,901
Want me to turn myself in
over a knife fight?

423
00:41:07,027 --> 00:41:08,362
Well, it worked out.

424
00:41:08,445 --> 00:41:10,698
It's a forced retirement.

425
00:41:10,781 --> 00:41:12,032
Right? I'm old too.

426
00:41:13,117 --> 00:41:15,202
The karma I built up with my fists.

427
00:41:15,286 --> 00:41:17,371
I'm paying it off with one arm.

428
00:41:17,454 --> 00:41:18,872
Then what are you gonna do now?

429
00:41:21,542 --> 00:41:23,877
You punk, since when do you care about me?

430
00:41:25,045 --> 00:41:26,046
Are we close, punk?

431
00:41:26,964 --> 00:41:28,757
Well, it's partly my fault.

432
00:41:30,634 --> 00:41:32,177
I'm trying to help you now.

433
00:41:32,261 --> 00:41:33,721
Cut the bullshit. Damn it.

434
00:41:35,598 --> 00:41:38,976
I don't need help from a punk like you.

435
00:41:43,355 --> 00:41:44,481
Anyway…

436
00:41:45,065 --> 00:41:46,358
So,

437
00:41:47,568 --> 00:41:49,570
are you the fake one or the real one?

438
00:42:04,918 --> 00:42:06,629
That fire on the school trip.

439
00:42:10,049 --> 00:42:11,383
I started that fire.

440
00:42:16,472 --> 00:42:19,683
I remember everything
now that I'm off the meds.

441
00:42:21,852 --> 00:42:23,604
I was the one who started the fire.

442
00:42:25,022 --> 00:42:25,981
Why'd you do it?

443
00:42:27,107 --> 00:42:30,027
Something happened
the day before the school trip.

444
00:42:30,110 --> 00:42:32,863
CHEONGUN CRAM SCHOOL
FOR MIDDLE AND HIGH SCHOOL STUDENTS

445
00:42:32,946 --> 00:42:34,782
Who's Park Chan-u?

446
00:42:37,993 --> 00:42:40,245
Why'd you register under a different name?

447
00:42:43,999 --> 00:42:45,125
Don't like your name?

448
00:42:46,835 --> 00:42:47,670
I don't.

449
00:42:48,420 --> 00:42:49,505
Why?

450
00:42:50,422 --> 00:42:53,884
It doesn't feel like my name.
I don't want to live with it.

451
00:42:53,967 --> 00:42:55,260
How come?

452
00:42:57,262 --> 00:43:01,600
You have to be a better Je Moon-jae
than the old Moon-jae.

453
00:43:03,727 --> 00:43:06,647
Whether at home or at school,

454
00:43:06,730 --> 00:43:08,941
I had nothing to show for it.

455
00:43:09,024 --> 00:43:11,652
You know, nothing special.

456
00:43:12,653 --> 00:43:14,571
I was neither this nor that.

457
00:43:15,155 --> 00:43:18,200
I think that's why my mom and father
didn't like me.

458
00:43:20,327 --> 00:43:22,079
I didn't like myself for it either.

459
00:43:23,247 --> 00:43:26,875
So I guess I wanted to be different
that night.

460
00:43:29,378 --> 00:43:30,963
Like being reborn, I guess?

461
00:43:31,463 --> 00:43:32,548
You know,

462
00:43:33,048 --> 00:43:38,512
a kid who would only cross on green,
even when no cars were coming,

463
00:43:39,513 --> 00:43:44,101
became someone who could cross on red
for the first time that night.

464
00:43:46,854 --> 00:43:48,772
It was like a reset button.

465
00:43:49,273 --> 00:43:50,399
That fire.

466
00:43:50,482 --> 00:43:51,692
So,

467
00:43:52,818 --> 00:43:54,611
did you switch names again?

468
00:43:56,989 --> 00:43:58,490
You crazy bastard.

469
00:43:58,574 --> 00:44:00,075
What choice did I have?

470
00:44:00,659 --> 00:44:01,660
I have to live too.

471
00:44:01,744 --> 00:44:03,829
Fucking bastard.

472
00:44:15,966 --> 00:44:16,800
Noja.

473
00:44:19,052 --> 00:44:20,429
Can I stay with you?

474
00:44:23,015 --> 00:44:24,641
I've got no one but you now.

475
00:44:26,602 --> 00:44:28,270
Stop bullshitting.

476
00:44:28,771 --> 00:44:30,147
I'm not your friend.

477
00:44:30,647 --> 00:44:31,899
Not taking the money?

478
00:44:33,192 --> 00:44:34,401
What money?

479
00:44:35,736 --> 00:44:36,987
Your money.

480
00:44:37,571 --> 00:44:39,239
I can give it back to you.

481
00:44:39,323 --> 00:44:40,491
Take the money.

482
00:44:46,121 --> 00:44:47,498
That's not my money.

483
00:44:49,541 --> 00:44:52,419
I told you before, didn't I?

484
00:44:52,920 --> 00:44:54,963
No matter how shitty your life is,

485
00:44:56,673 --> 00:44:59,051
you've got to be the real one.

486
00:45:01,804 --> 00:45:03,639
Seung-gyu will come looking for you.

487
00:45:05,516 --> 00:45:09,228
That bastard's not the type
to give up on his money.

488
00:45:10,395 --> 00:45:11,897
Don't go wandering around.

489
00:45:11,980 --> 00:45:13,440
Stay hidden.

490
00:45:13,941 --> 00:45:15,317
If he catches you,

491
00:45:16,401 --> 00:45:17,986
you won't die easy.

492
00:45:26,578 --> 00:45:27,913
Where are you buying smokes?

493
00:45:30,415 --> 00:45:31,750
Over there.

494
00:45:37,923 --> 00:45:41,385
Why do you wear fake glasses? You dumbass.

495
00:45:49,184 --> 00:45:50,602
The light changed.

496
00:45:50,686 --> 00:45:51,603
Get lost.

497
00:46:51,413 --> 00:46:52,331
Just…

498
00:46:52,414 --> 00:46:53,540
Just a moment.

499
00:47:00,631 --> 00:47:04,927
THE RAT

500
00:47:21,818 --> 00:47:22,653
THE RAT
VOLUME TWO

501
00:47:24,363 --> 00:47:27,991
Volumes one and two
are usually released together.

502
00:47:28,492 --> 00:47:32,663
Since volume two wasn't finished in time,
we released volume one first.

503
00:47:33,330 --> 00:47:37,417
Readers are going crazy right now.

504
00:47:38,543 --> 00:47:41,338
Volume two needs to come out soon.
They are waiting for it.

505
00:47:43,882 --> 00:47:44,841
We

506
00:47:45,342 --> 00:47:47,594
might become really famous.

507
00:47:47,678 --> 00:47:49,638
Hurry home and finish editing it.

508
00:47:52,432 --> 00:47:54,393
Apartment 705, Luchena Tower, Gangnam.

509
00:47:55,352 --> 00:47:58,605
The passcode is 0912.
You know that, right?

510
00:49:00,167 --> 00:49:03,295
I LOATHE EVERYTHING ABOUT YOU…
THE RAT

511
00:49:04,129 --> 00:49:05,964
This story is entirely true.

512
00:49:07,466 --> 00:49:09,301
I killed someone.

513
00:49:10,260 --> 00:49:13,555
This is a record of my crime
and a letter of confession.

514
00:49:14,890 --> 00:49:17,976
This is proof that I'm the Rat.

515
00:49:29,321 --> 00:49:30,989
Wait, this…

516
00:49:37,829 --> 00:49:38,747
No.

517
00:49:39,539 --> 00:49:40,373
This…

518
00:49:41,166 --> 00:49:43,043
This should never get out.

519
00:49:43,126 --> 00:49:44,127
This…

520
00:49:44,753 --> 00:49:48,006
This is proof I'm the Rat, not a human.

521
00:49:49,174 --> 00:49:50,759
This isn't the end.

522
00:49:51,259 --> 00:49:53,553
You won't be able to handle it.

523
00:49:55,055 --> 00:49:58,100
DEFENDANT

524
00:49:58,183 --> 00:49:59,101
Mr. Park.

525
00:49:59,601 --> 00:50:02,187
Is there anything you'd like to add?

526
00:50:05,065 --> 00:50:06,942
PLAINTIFF

527
00:50:10,112 --> 00:50:11,780
I recently found my uncle.

528
00:50:13,281 --> 00:50:15,283
He's not related to me by blood,

529
00:50:16,451 --> 00:50:19,454
and I barely remembered him.

530
00:50:21,581 --> 00:50:23,834
But when I was little,

531
00:50:25,043 --> 00:50:26,753
he was like a father to me.

532
00:50:27,629 --> 00:50:30,382
He's already at the tail end of his life.

533
00:50:32,134 --> 00:50:33,844
Seeing him again

534
00:50:35,637 --> 00:50:39,141
made me think about

535
00:50:40,058 --> 00:50:40,892
what family means.

536
00:50:45,856 --> 00:50:47,065
I remember…

537
00:50:49,067 --> 00:50:53,155
reading the phrase
"the beginning of the end"

538
00:50:53,780 --> 00:50:55,907
somewhere a long time ago.

539
00:50:56,491 --> 00:50:57,826
The thing is,

540
00:50:58,660 --> 00:51:02,289
I'm not very smart,
so I don't know exactly what it means.

541
00:51:02,372 --> 00:51:03,915
But I thought…

542
00:51:07,377 --> 00:51:10,172
it didn't mean that the end was beginning…

543
00:51:12,799 --> 00:51:15,343
but that things begin at the end.

544
00:51:16,970 --> 00:51:20,265
That was just how I interpreted it
back then.

545
00:51:21,808 --> 00:51:25,729
I know it's because I failed
as a husband and father

546
00:51:25,812 --> 00:51:28,940
that my family has come
to the end of the road

547
00:51:30,775 --> 00:51:31,610
like this.

548
00:51:33,612 --> 00:51:34,446
But if…

549
00:51:36,740 --> 00:51:38,158
at the end of this road…

550
00:51:39,576 --> 00:51:41,578
I'm given one last chance…

551
00:51:45,207 --> 00:51:46,082
If you can…

552
00:51:48,710 --> 00:51:50,086
If I could…

553
00:51:53,006 --> 00:51:54,507
somehow get that chance,

554
00:51:55,008 --> 00:51:56,092
I…

555
00:51:58,220 --> 00:51:59,930
I'd like to start over.

556
00:52:00,013 --> 00:52:02,891
MEDIATION JUDGE

557
00:52:10,148 --> 00:52:11,107
If I were given…

558
00:52:14,653 --> 00:52:16,446
one last chance.

559
00:53:23,013 --> 00:53:23,888
Hey!

560
00:53:31,896 --> 00:53:32,731
You're here?

561
00:53:32,814 --> 00:53:34,566
It's so hot today, so…

562
00:53:34,649 --> 00:53:36,276
Don't just stand there.

563
00:53:36,359 --> 00:53:37,944
If you're here, help out.

564
00:53:38,028 --> 00:53:41,740
I need to tend to that dying one
and pick and dry the chili peppers.

565
00:53:41,823 --> 00:53:43,074
Perfect timing.

566
00:53:43,158 --> 00:53:44,534
Go change and come back.

567
00:54:46,721 --> 00:54:48,431
The Rat thought

568
00:54:49,057 --> 00:54:52,352
that it could never escape from here.

569
00:54:53,937 --> 00:54:55,271
The perfect rathole.

570
00:54:55,939 --> 00:54:58,733
There would be no place safer than here.

571
00:54:58,817 --> 00:54:59,901
But…

572
00:55:01,027 --> 00:55:02,028
But

573
00:55:03,613 --> 00:55:07,492
after weeks of agonizing recollection,

574
00:55:08,368 --> 00:55:11,454
the Rat finally realized
that it was that loathsome Rat.

575
00:55:13,998 --> 00:55:15,333
Everything was a dream.

576
00:55:17,001 --> 00:55:19,295
A dream made by endless self-loathing.

577
00:55:24,300 --> 00:55:27,178
There wasn't a shred of truth in it.

578
00:55:28,304 --> 00:55:29,514
It had gone insane.

579
00:55:30,014 --> 00:55:31,975
Even dreams and reality…

580
00:55:32,058 --> 00:55:33,977
HAN JI-HYE, EDITOR-IN-CHIEF
WE CAN'T WAIT ANYMORE!

581
00:55:34,060 --> 00:55:35,437
No!

582
00:55:35,520 --> 00:55:36,521
Fuck.

583
00:55:37,105 --> 00:55:38,690
No. Fuck.

584
00:55:38,773 --> 00:55:39,899
Just wait!

585
00:55:59,461 --> 00:56:01,504
Who is it? What kind of fucking…

586
00:56:06,134 --> 00:56:07,719
Fuck off!

587
00:56:08,720 --> 00:56:10,930
I said fuck off! You fucking bastards.

588
00:56:15,685 --> 00:56:16,603
Try and come in.

589
00:56:17,103 --> 00:56:19,272
Try and come in! You fucking bastards!

590
00:57:24,170 --> 00:57:27,131
How have you been, you fucking bastard?

591
00:57:30,385 --> 00:57:32,053
Didn't think I'd find you, did you?

592
00:57:33,304 --> 00:57:35,139
Open the door, you fucking bastard.

593
00:57:36,349 --> 00:57:39,686
I said open the door, you fucking bastard!

594
00:57:52,615 --> 00:57:54,158
Hey, rat bastard.

595
00:57:55,243 --> 00:57:57,328
I know you're hiding in there.

596
00:57:59,414 --> 00:58:02,083
Hey, we've got to settle this money issue,

597
00:58:03,668 --> 00:58:05,878
or this is never going to end.

598
00:58:07,589 --> 00:58:09,674
Hey, rat bastard. Open the door now.

599
00:58:10,800 --> 00:58:13,094
I said open the door, you fucking bastard!

600
00:58:15,013 --> 00:58:17,849
MOUSETRAP

